<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n19172" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Βάκχ-ειος</span></b>  or <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Βακχεῖος</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">α</span>, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span>, also <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Βάκχιος</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">α</span>, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span> (to suit the metre), fem. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ος</span>
		<i><span class="en">
			Luc.
			<u>Ocyp.</u>
			171
		</span></i>:—<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>of</i> or
				<i>belonging to Bacchus</i> and <i>his rites,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">βότρυς</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					S.
					<u>Fr.</u>
					255.2
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">νόμος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					E.
					<u>Hec.</u>
					686
				</span></i>
			 (lyr.); 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ῥυθμός</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					X.
					<u>Smp.</u>
					9.3
				</span></i>
			, etc.: hence, <i>frenzied, rapt,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Β. Διόνυσος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>h.Hom.</u>
					19.46
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Hdt.
				4.79
			</span></i>; ὁ
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Β. θεός</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					S.
					<u>OT</u>
					1105
				</span></i>
			 (lyr.); 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Βάκχειε δεσπότ᾽</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Ar.
					<u>Th.</u>
					988
				</span></i>
			 (lyr.), cf. <i><span class="en">
				<u>IG</u>
				4.558.20
			</span></i> (<span class="entity">Argos</span>), etc.; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὸν</span>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Β. ἄνακτα,</span> of Aeschylus, <i><span class="en">
				Ar.
				<u>Ra.</u>
				1259
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b> as
				Subst., <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Βάκχιος, ὁ,</span>
			
				=
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Βάκχος</span>
			, <i><span class="en">
				S.
				<u>Ant.</u>
				154
			</span></i> (lyr.), <i><span class="en">
				E.
				<u>Cyc.</u>
				9
			</span></i>:—also, 
				=
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οἶνος</span>
			, <i><span class="en">
				Id.
				<u>IT</u>
				953
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>Cyc.</u>
				519
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Antiph.
				237
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Βάκχια</span></b>  or <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Βακχ-εῖα</span></b> , τά, 
				v.
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Βακχεῖον.</span>
			
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>3.</b>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Βακχεῖος</span> (sc. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πούς</span>), ὁ,
				<i>the bacchius, a metrical foot of three syllables,</i> _ _
			^, <i><span class="en">
				D.H.
				<u>Comp.</u>
				17
			</span></i> (opp. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὑποβ.</span> ^ _ _); but
			later ^ _ _, <i><span class="en">
				Heph.
				3
			</span></i> (opp. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">παλιμβ.</span> _ _ ^), etc.;
			also <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">β. ἀπὸ τροχαίου</span> (_ ^ ^ _),
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀπ᾽ ἰάμβου</span> (^ _ _ ^), <i><span class="en">
				Aristid.Quint.
				1.17
			</span></i>, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Anon.Rhythm.
				<u>Oxy.</u>
				9 iii 12
			</span></i>; = ^ ^ _ _, <i><span class="en">
				Bacch.
				<u>Harm.</u>
				101
			</span></i>.</div>
